# Source is stored with LF and checked out however the platform prefers.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Profile fixtures are byte-exact test data, not text. Line-ending
# normalisation would change their length and their content between platforms,
# which is precisely what a parser test corpus must not do. Real Xdebug output
# on Windows also legitimately contains CRLF, and that is part of what these
# files exist to prove the parser survives.
fixtures/callgrind/** -text -diff
